# bead 8f3 (P1): LibreLane 2.4.13 post-GRT STA (OpenROAD.STAMidPNR-3) runs on unannotated
# (zero-wire) parasitics, making post-GRT timing/power figures optimistic -- possibly including
# run 23's accepted post-GRT sign-off. Found under w3a.
#
# Root cause: sta/corner.tcl's `if { [grt::have_routes] }` branch calls
# `estimate_parasitics -global_routing` on a freshly read_current_odb ODB whose routing-guide
# data is only PERSISTED (from an earlier GlobalRouting step), not live in this process. Per
# bead je8 (bd memory openroad-grt-parasitics-need-insession-route), OpenROAD cannot recover
# real GRT parasitics from that persisted state alone -- it needs a live in-session
# global_route. Confirmed empirically in this bead on a real ASAP7 CPU block: 34272/36290
# drivers (94.44%) unannotated, and the resulting "post-GRT" STA falsely reports ZERO setup and
# hold violations everywhere (WNS=0, TNS=0, 0 violators on both).
#
# Two independent, backward-compatible pieces:
#
#   1. STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT (bool, default false) -- when true, corner.tcl sources
#      common/grt.tcl (the SAME routing-layer / layer-adjustment / global_route setup the
#      GlobalRouting step itself uses) immediately before estimate_parasitics -global_routing.
#      Unset is BYTE-IDENTICAL to upstream. Declared identically on THREE step classes
#      (OpenROAD.STAMidPNR, MultiCornerSTA, OpenROAD.ResizerTimingPostGRT) because all three
#      share the same Classic flow and Flow.get_all_config_variables() raises FlowException on
#      any same-named Variable with a field mismatch across steps in one flow -- but the
#      variable is CONSULTED only in corner.tcl (used by OpenROAD.STAMidPNR). It is inert on
#      MultiCornerSTA-derived steps (STAPrePNR/STAPostPNR run corner.tcl through the standalone
#      `sta` binary, never `openroad`, so the whole grt::have_routes/-global_routing branch is
#      unreachable there) and inert on OpenROAD.ResizerTimingPostGRT, which ALREADY sources
#      common/grt.tcl unconditionally today (a pre-existing "Temporarily always enabled" upstream
#      workaround, see rsz_timing_postgrt.tcl) -- gating that existing behaviour behind a
#      default-false variable would be a REGRESSION, so it was deliberately left alone.
#      `grt_variables` (GRT_ADJUSTMENT, GRT_OVERFLOW_ITERS, GRT_ALLOW_CONGESTION,
#      GRT_MACRO_EXTENSION, RT_MIN/MAX_LAYER, etc.) also had to be added to STAMidPNR's own
#      config_vars -- undeclared variables are silently dropped during config resolution, so
#      `source common/grt.tcl`'s own dependencies would otherwise never reach _env.tcl (a real
#      failure hit and fixed during this bead's own validation: `can't read
#      "::env(GRT_ADJUSTMENT)": no such variable`). OpenROAD.GlobalRouting and ResizerStep
#      (ResizerTimingPostCTS/PostGRT's base) already carry grt_variables for the same reason --
#      that is WHY rsz_timing_postgrt.tcl's existing re-route already worked.
#
#   2. An ALWAYS-ON annotation gate (`ol_check_postgrt_parasitic_annotation`, new proc in
#      common/io.tcl) -- called from corner.tcl (inside the -global_routing branch ONLY, never
#      the -placement branch, so placement-stage STA is unaffected) and unconditionally from
#      rsz_timing_postgrt.tcl (right after its own long-standing estimate_parasitics
#      -global_routing). Captures `report_parasitic_annotation -report_unannotated`'s output via
#      Tcl's generic `> file` redirect support (confirmed present in report_parasitic_annotation's
#      own body on both toolchains), regexes "Found N unannotated drivers.", and computes a
#      percentage against `[llength [get_cells -hierarchical *]]` as a cheap PROXY for "total
#      drivers" (multi-output cells make this approximate, not exact -- documented inline).
#      Prints a loud [WARNING] naming STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT above
#      STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_PCT_MAX (env-read directly, default 1.0%; a secondary tuning knob,
#      not a declared Variable) or exits 1 if STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_IS_ERROR=1. This is NOT
#      gated behind STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT -- it always runs and always reports, whether or
#      not the caller has opted into the fix, so a broken run is loud rather than silent.
#
# Validation (bead 8f3, 2026-09-16), full run-by-run detail on the bead:
#   - valu_rtl (never reaches corner.tcl's openroad-binary path) unset: byte-identical to the
#     pre-8f3 baseline.
#   - ASAP7 CPU block (rv32i_cpu_top, 10 SRAM macros), fresh full runs to OpenROAD.STAMidPNR-3:
#       UNSET (bpp-6): Flow complete. 34272/36290 (94.44%) unannotated, gate WARNING fired.
#         Resulting STA falsely clean: setup/hold WNS=0, TNS=0, 0 violators either direction.
#       SET STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT=1 (bpp-7): Flow complete. 619/36290 (1.71%) unannotated --
#         matches this project's established benign SRAM-stub floor (the same 619 count
#         ResizerTimingPostGRT already reports every run) rather than a remaining bug. Real,
#         differing STA: setup WNS -169.722 ps, TNS -70913.1 ps, 1008 violators; hold stays
#         clean (WNS 15.88 ps, 0 violators). STAMidPNR-3 runtime nearly unchanged (~61s both
#         ways); peak RSS grew ~515 MiB -> ~810 MiB (+~295 MiB) for the in-session re-route on
#         this CPU-block-scale design -- far below the "5.4 GB peak / 24 min" quoted for the full
#         SoC under bead je8, as expected for a much smaller design.
#   - rsz_timing_postgrt.tcl's own gate (item 3 of the task): 619/36206 (1.71%) unannotated in
#     BOTH bpp-6 and bpp-7 (unaffected by STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT, as expected since that
#     variable is inert there) -- confirms its pre-existing unconditional re-route was already
#     keeping it correctly annotated; it never had this bead's problem.
#   - NOT re-validated by this bead: historical accepted post-GRT figures (run 23, earlier 86a)
#     were produced with the OLD, un-gated corner.tcl and remain unaudited. Follow-up work.
#
# Base: relative to the live tree's state immediately before this bead's apply, i.e. AFTER both
# prior bpp patches (librelane2413_sta_26q2_scenes.diff, librelane2413_resizer_timing_bounds.diff)
# and all earlier local patches. Apply after those.

diff -u a/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl b/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl
--- a/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl	2026-09-15 23:41:26.040097496 +0700
+++ b/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl	2026-09-16 05:47:38.411576210 +0700
@@ -51,6 +51,58 @@
     return [$c name]
 }
 
+# claude_verilog_test local patch (bead 8f3, 2026-09-16): post-GRT parasitic annotation gate.
+# OpenROAD edf00dff (and, per this bead's own re-check, 26Q2 too) cannot recover real GRT
+# parasitics from a saved ODB's persisted routing guides -- estimate_parasitics -global_routing
+# after a fresh read_current_odb leaves almost every driver UNANNOTATED (zero-wire), silently,
+# unless global_route is re-run IN-SESSION first (bead je8 / bd memory
+# openroad-grt-parasitics-need-insession-route). This proc is ALWAYS run (no gating variable)
+# right after any `estimate_parasitics -global_routing` call, so a broken/optimistic post-GRT
+# STA or resizer run is loud rather than silent, regardless of whether the caller has also
+# opted into an in-session re-route. It deliberately does nothing for -placement-based
+# estimates (mid-flow, pre-route STA), which were never claiming GRT-derived parasitics in the
+# first place and are unaffected by this bead.
+#
+# "total drivers" here is a cheap proxy (instance count via `get_cells -hierarchical *`), since
+# report_parasitic_annotation does not itself print a total -- multi-output cells make this an
+# approximation, not an exact driver-pin count, but it is stable and good enough for a percentage
+# threshold gate. STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_PCT_MAX (default 1.0, i.e. 1%) and
+# STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_IS_ERROR (default off) are read directly from ::env rather than
+# declared Variables, since they are secondary tuning knobs for this always-on gate, not the
+# primary opt-in behaviour switch (that is STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT, which IS a declared
+# Variable -- see steps/openroad.py).
+proc ol_check_postgrt_parasitic_annotation {} {
+    set rpt_path [file join $::env(STEP_DIR) "_bead_8f3_parasitic_annotation_check.rpt"]
+    if { [catch {report_parasitic_annotation -report_unannotated > $rpt_path} err] } {
+        puts stderr "\[WARNING\] bead 8f3: report_parasitic_annotation failed, cannot check post-GRT annotation coverage: $err"
+        return
+    }
+    set fp [open $rpt_path r]
+    set txt [read $fp]
+    close $fp
+    puts $txt
+    set unannotated 0
+    regexp {Found\s+(\d+)\s+unannotated drivers\.} $txt -> unannotated
+    set total_drivers [llength [get_cells -hierarchical *]]
+    if { $total_drivers <= 0 || $unannotated <= 0 } {
+        return
+    }
+    set pct [expr { 100.0 * $unannotated / double($total_drivers) }]
+    set threshold 1.0
+    if { [info exists ::env(STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_PCT_MAX)] && $::env(STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_PCT_MAX) != "" } {
+        set threshold $::env(STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_PCT_MAX)
+    }
+    if { $pct > $threshold } {
+        set msg "bead 8f3: $unannotated/$total_drivers drivers (~[format %.2f $pct]%) are UNANNOTATED after estimate_parasitics -global_routing -- post-GRT STA/power numbers are likely zero-wire and optimistic. Set STA_POSTGRT_INSESSION_GRT=1 to force an in-session global_route before parasitics estimation (see memory/pd/knowledge.md)."
+        if { [info exists ::env(STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_IS_ERROR)] && $::env(STA_POSTGRT_UNANNOTATED_IS_ERROR) == 1 } {
+            puts stderr "\[ERROR\] $msg"
+            exit 1
+        } else {
+            puts stderr "\[WARNING\] $msg"
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 proc string_in_file {file_path substring} {
     set f [open $file_path r]
     set data [read $f]

